cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LiteMLflow in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "LiteMLflow: Single-binary MLflow-compatible experiment tracker"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-05-08"
url: "https://github.com/litemlflow/litemlflow"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/litemlflow/litemlflow"
abstract: >
  LiteMLflow is a lightweight, self-hosted experiment tracker for machine learning
  and LLM workflows. It is compatible with the MLflow REST API (~80% of the
  canonical surface), ships as a single statically-linked Go binary with zero
  runtime dependencies, and adds first-class support for LLM traces, versioned
  prompts, and evals. The server starts in ~53 ms (143× faster cold start vs
  MLflow + SQLite) and stores all data in SQLite + local filesystem, enabling
  single-command backup and restore.
